# SOURCE direction v3.0

Canonical document: `docs/SOURCE-PRODUCT-ENGINEERING-DIRECTION-v3.md`

SOURCE is **The Missing Information Engine**. Promise: we find what's missing, then we resolve it. DPP is the first urgent use-case, not the product ceiling.

Do not interpret the direction doc as permission to implement every section. Audit sections 12–20 and 33–40 first. Preserve prototype acceptance-test semantics. No unrelated features.

## Frozen

- Domain: InformationRequirement → ResolutionCase → ResolutionAttempt(s) → Readiness Gates
- READY requires IDENTITY, VALUE, EVIDENCE, SCOPE, VALIDITY, PERMISSION, CONFLICT
- Never ask a supplier for information SOURCE can already resolve
- Server-side authz, capability tokens, confidentiality policies
- Canonical identity before any propagation; search then evaluate, never copy claims across tenants
- React consumes the engine; it does not own business truth

## Hypotheses (do not freeze)

- Stripe is the source of list prices and entitlements. Do not hardcode €99/€249/€599/€999 as truth.
- First vertical (industrial / construction / furniture) is a research priority, not a proven market.
- GO/PIVOT/KILL percentages are an internal rubric after real manufacturer pilots.

## Build now (P0)

Security boundary, persistence, supplier capability tokens, idempotency, readiness invariants, canonical identity, resolution propagation, event/audit log, seed/test isolation.

## Do not build

Blockchain, complex graphs, generic PIM/PLM, DPP designer, marketplace, ESG dashboard, dozens of regulations, 10 ERP connectors, mobile app, AI chatbot, Supplier Pro, marketing site as engine substitute.

Priority: Security boundary → persistence → idempotency → invariants → canonical identity → resolution propagation → readiness scan → resolution planner.

Goal of this phase: a production-safe resolution engine that can prove or falsify autonomous information resolution with real manufacturer data. Not a production DPP SaaS.
